  "details": "i would like to see a proper implementation of the xinput system, so far it seems it only sends keyboard inputs to the client.\n\nuse cases are :\n\n1- navigating the cameras around in fly-mode without having to use the mouse button to trigger said mode (mostly a desktop issue, but i can see also vr user wanting to take an xbox controller to exclusively move the camera without having to toggle a fly-mode, retaining the ability to move themselves, while not moving the camera)\n\n2- any xinput compliant device would be able to take advantage of it: in the example of the camera, you could use a flightstick to control PTZ like we do in real world. make it a toggle inside the camera to that it takes exclusive input from the controller and the base movement doesn't get affected\n\n3- any world that use driving/vehicle could take advantage of the analog nature of the thumbstick/pressure instead of a simple keyboard input\n\n4- i can think of other ideas, but im sure having an exclusive xinput mode that can be detached from the base WASD movements wil give a lot of creative opportunities to world builder, avatar creator, and third party content creators (such as myself and other streamers)\n\ni can elaborate with ideas and concept if this gets traction, but i want to keep this to the point of \"what needs to work on\" before giving too many ideas out there that will influence how this feature gets implemented. we want options to work with, not necessarly hardcoded use-cases",
